    "name": "book_slope_delta_60s",
    "mechanism": "Book-shape dynamics: the 60s change of book_slope - whether the price-depth profile is actively STEEPENING or FLATTENING. The shape level says where the book is; its delta says where it is going. Active steepening toward one side means limit-order flow is currently building an asymmetric profile (fresh one-sided positioning -> continuation of that side), flattening means commitment is being withdrawn across levels (pressure dissipates). Shape can move without total bid/ask imbalance moving (depth migrating between levels), so this derivative is orthogonal to the wdi/depth5 deltas by construction.",
